==Strategy==
Whereas on the first two stages you were able to stall for money and prepare your units, to emphasize Poultrio's extremely unfair enemy design, this stage throws Poultrio at you after less than 30 seconds of being in the stage. While this stage does supply you with a cash supply, that being Devil Wife, this time it's actually dangerous since the Death Surge risks your units being wiped out. Alongside extremely annoying peons like Gabriels and Mr. Angel which pose an actual risk to your Dodge meatshields thanks to their damage, a Medu-san whose rapid Surges are able to hit your backliner such as Mewtone, infinite Condemned Pengs and Heavenly Hippoes which can take quite the punishment before going down, and a timed St. Dober who is extremely hard to control alongside Poultrio, this stage pulls absolutely no punches. St. Dober in particular is extremely dangerous, given that your Dodge meatshields will be one shot by his Surges, allowing Poultrio to speedrun towards your base and get you to lose. Try to kill the Devil Wives as fast as you can for a quick cash supply alongside the usage of a Rich Cat, then lure Poultrio and beat it down while trying to kill every supporting enemy with whatever you have in your lineup.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Dodge]] meatshields: You will need Dodge meatshields to even stand a chance against Poultrio's extremely rapid and powerful attacks. Examples include [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]], [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]], Talented [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Flying Ninja Cat]], and a Talented [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]]. For this stage specifically, you can get away with Bellydance by herself, although you will want to boost her. She's quite expensive, so pairing her up with a cheap meatshield like Ninja or Brainwashed Mohawk is helpful. Do not only use Dodge meatshields here, as you will lose immediately once St. Dober enters the field.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Rock is required to bring along on its stage due to its blazing fast speed and recharge and powerful stalling potential, making it extremely helpful to stall Poultrio. Use Boulder carefully, as Rock is able to bait out more St. Dober Surges and get him to wipe everything out.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train is very useful on these stages if luck is on your side. Depending on how many times Poultrio decides to launch Knockbacks, it can land a bunch of extra damage and brute force the Shield. It also works well in sniping the Sinner Snaches, Gabriels, and Mr. Angels for quick cash injections.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Cyberpunk and Deadeye are needed perhaps the most for this stage in particular, as if you have no Ubers St. Dober is extremely hard to control. Deadeye in particular has Knockback, forcing Dober back and preventing him from attacking your meatshields. Deadeye may be safely sent out when Medu-san appears, as long as you have managed to get a few damage knockbacks on Poultrio so that he isn't directly near your base.
*[[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Mewtone]]: Mewtone is an immeasurably powerful super-backliner whose long Slow vs. Red helps out considerably against the boss, and Mewtone's high damage makes him perfect to chip down the other enemies. While Mewtone will die to Medu-san, Mewtone is so cracked for this stage that you can risk having him die here.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]]: Uril and his True Form are required for this stage with his powerful anti-Aku crowd-control, which can disable Poultrio's extremely annoying Knockback and Slow him very well and allow him to deal with Condemned Peng and chip away against Medu-san.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Bahamut isn't really good on Poultrio because Poultrio doesn't have the fake attack compared to the other R. Ost variants, but you can use him if you use a Thunderbolt on Poultrio and Medu-san beforehand to get huge amounts of damage off. Just know that this doesn't work nearly as well against St. Dober thanks to Dober having a huge healthpool.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultimate Thundia β]]: Thundia lacks immunities to Poultrio, but her massive nuke damage to Poultrio allows her to ignore those issues. With a multi-hit which can both brute-force the Shield and get a damage knockback onto Poultrio, using Thundia you can get a quick clear of the stage. What puts Thundia over the edge compared to almost every other Uber option for this stage, however, is her being able to abuse Poultrio's Knockbacks to the fullest: often, Thundia will get her first, more damaging hit off on Poultrio, thus either landing a damage knockback or brute-forcing its Shield, then get knocked back by Poultrio, thus allowing her to start her attack again.
*Ultra Talented [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: With her Target Aku and HP Buff Talents, Kai is able to wall the boss and Medu-san immensely, and her high damage and Shield Piercing Talent can also get a decent chunk out onto the boss. Her health will go down surprisingly quick when Dober is on the field, however.
*[[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Phantasmal Nobunaga]]: A single Phantasmal Nobunaga hit onto an unshielded Poultrio can cripple Poultrio for a huge amount of time, and alongside other DPS options to constantly break Poultrio's Shield you can get a huge amount of damage off. Given the fact that Medu-san and other Surgers are present here, Nobunaga's Counter-Surge can get crazy value and allow the sickest Bahamut chains you will see in your whole life. Similarly, [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]] also has a lengthy Freeze, although with a shorter foreswing and a shorter Freeze. If you have Ice Cat's Ultra Talents for whatever reason, her Dodge Talent is a considerable help for this stage, and her Strengthen Talent can allow her to dish out a pretty good amount of damage.
*[[Uesugi Kenshin (Uber Rare Cat)|Hellrider Kenshin]]: Kenshin's good health and double Knockback with her Mini-Wave allows her to push Poultrio to the base as well as chip away at the supporting enemies with said Mini-Wave. Be careful using her, as you can easily get Uril to miss his attack if using her.
**[[Imagawa Yoshimoto (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yoshimoto]]: If you have Yoshimoto's Ultra Talents, he clowns on this stage entirely thanks to his Counter-Surge allowing him to completely nuke Poultrio.
*[[The White Rabbit (Uber Rare Cat)|The Spectral Cat]]: Spectral's high effective health and damage makes her a really good Uber for Poultrio, as well as having some incredibly powerful CC in the form of a lengthy Slow and crippling Weaken which can easily combo with Uril and Mewtone. As a bonus, her initial hit is able to brute-force Poultrio's Shield, and her second and third hits will then apply the Weaken and Slow onto Poultrio.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Cosmo, when protected well, can get huge value here thanks to him making Dober a non-issue.
*Ultra Talented [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Anubis]]: If you have Anubis's Ultra Talents for whatever reason, he is an extremely viable option for this stage thanks to his Knockback Immunity, chance of piercing Shields, Surge Immunity, and high DPS, alongside an unreliable Surge which can nuke a supporting enemy if it actually lands. However, given Poultrio's extremely aggressive nature, the playstyle of luring into Anubis's range to allow his attack to connect is very risky thanks to his long foreswing.
*[[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Lucifer]]: Especially with his Target Angel Talent, Lucifer gets good value here as a sniper able to get high damage against the supporting threats.
*[[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Beartooth]]: With its Dodge Talent, B.C.S. Beartooth becomes an incredibly powerful anti-Poultrio nuker able to deal huge amounts of damage onto Poultrio while also having Knockback Immunity and a decent chance to dodge Poultrio's attacks. The Dodge Talent in particular is what makes Beartooth so strong here, being able to withstand a bunch of Poultrio hits while dishing out crazy damage that can remove high amounts of the boss's health.
*[[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-03 Cloud Emperor]]: Bomburr's Ultra Form isn't the greatest backliner generalist to exist, but even if Untalented, Bomburr's Explosions, if they occur, can force damage knockbacks onto the supporting enemies. The main appeal of Bomburr's Ultra Form, though, is its Explosion Immunity, allowing it to stay on the field for a decent amount of time before it finally goes down.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Phonoa's ridiculous effective DPS and high range allows them to stand safely in the backline as long as your defense is good and chip away at Poultrio and the supporting enemies. To an extent, [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] also does the same job, albeit with a bit more risk as their rather short Slow (2 secs) can override longer Slow effects, like that of Mewtone.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Lunacia's excellent crowd-control and damage to the boss makes her one of the strongest Uber options available for this Advent.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Death's Daughter Lunacia]]: Unlike her Uberfest counterpart, DLuna isn't as viable for Poultrio due to lower standing range and vulnerability to Knockback that may prevent her from attacking, but she's strong against all enemies here and has high health, so she can help with tanking some damage, and other enemies can serve as a stepping stone for her to attack or trigger Counter-Surges, dealing some damage as well as weakening enemies.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Luminous]]: Lunos isn't as great against Poultrio's stages compared to most other stages due to its Shield and really strong pushing power, but given that Lunos targets Aku and Angel, you can use him as a quick tanking option as well as for his Conjure for supporting enemy purposes. Just be careful of your cash, as you can easily go broke if there isn't a Devil Wife ready to die.
*[[Baki Hanma (Uber Rare Cat)|Baki Hanma]]: Baki is pretty good here with his high DPS, Explosion Immunity, short cooldown and rapid attacks allowing him to constantly Knockback Poultrio. As a bonus, Baki has a small chance to instantly Pierce Poultrio's Shield.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]]: Hanayama is usually super impractical to use thanks to his foreswing and tendency to miss, but given Medu-san's presence, you can use him here well enough to get huge damage off against Medu-san.
*[[Tanjiro Kamado (Uber Rare Cat)|Tanjiro Kamado]]: Tanjiro's general DPS is pretty bad, but when St. Dober comes in Tanjiro is able to get off some really nice damage.
*[[:Category:Cats with Knockback Immunity|Knockback-Immune]] Ubers: Quite a few Ubers have a Knockback Immunity Talent that often make them worse in almost every scenario possible. However, if you choose to purchase this Talent and thus make your Uber worse for the rest of the game, a lot of Ubers that previously would be deadweights thanks to Poultrio's constant Knockback and Explosion are now able to actually do a decent bit of work here. Examples include [[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]], [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]], [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Hevijak]], and [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]].
*[[Jeanne (Legend Rare Cat)|Divine Jeanne ψ]]: In her True Form, Jeanne gains buffs which allows her to work against Poultrio, although not fully counter it. Jeanne just so happens to stand 10 range away from Poultrio's Omni Strike and be Explosion-Immune, meaning that if you properly protect her she should theoretically be able to work as a really good Explosion-Immune nuker for the boss. However, the fact that she only outranges it by 10 means that you need to run support units like Uril, Mewtone, and have good meatshielding options to prevent her from getting destroyed by Poultrio.

